      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Combine the lamb mince, grated onion, garlic, parsley, cumin, coriander, smoked paprika, cinnamon, a generous pinch of salt and the black pepper in a large bowl. Mix well with your hands for 2 minutes until the mixture is uniform and slightly sticky."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Divide the mixture into 8 equal portions. Shape each one into a long oval around a flat metal skewer, pressing firmly so it grips. If using wooden skewers, soak them in water for 30 minutes first."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the griddle pan over a high heat until smoking. Brush lightly with a little oil."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cook the kofte in batches for 3 to 4 minutes per side without moving them, so they develop clear grill marks. They should be cooked through but still juicy."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Rest on a warm plate for 2 minutes. Serve with flatbreads, sliced tomato, red onion and a generous spoonful of plain yoghurt alongside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Kofte fall off the skewers"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Make sure you grate rather than chop the onion and squeeze out as much moisture as possible before mixing. Excess water stops the mixture binding. Chilling before cooking also helps."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Meat is dry and crumbly"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use lamb mince with at least 20% fat. Lean mince dries out quickly on a hot griddle. Do not overcook, and rest the kofte before serving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "No grill marks forming"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The griddle must be properly smoking hot before the kofte go on. Place them down and do not move them for a full 3 minutes. Moving too early tears the crust."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "You will find "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "kofte-term"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "kofte"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at every Turkish street food stall, grill restaurant and family table. The spice blend shifts subtly from region to region, but cumin, coriander and a touch of cinnamon are the backbone of the Turkish version. They are eaten wrapped in flatbread with tomato and onion, or alongside rice and grilled vegetables. The yoghurt alongside is not optional."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
